WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.010
- There you are, look at you.

00:00:02.010 --> 00:00:03.587
- You look beautiful.

00:00:03.587 --> 00:00:05.872
You're like glowing.

00:00:05.872 --> 00:00:07.787
- (laughing) You are so nuts.

00:00:07.787 --> 00:00:10.600
By the way, nothing makes me happier

00:00:10.600 --> 00:00:11.870
than watching you sing.

00:00:11.870 --> 00:00:13.825
I watch the whole thing
from the beginning.

00:00:13.825 --> 00:00:16.680
Nothing makes me happier
than listening to you

00:00:16.680 --> 00:00:20.430
say welcome to my show y'all, nothing.

00:00:20.430 --> 00:00:22.610
- You and Kathy called it years ago.

00:00:22.610 --> 00:00:24.270
You, you called it.

00:00:24.270 --> 00:00:25.103
Yeah.

00:00:25.103 --> 00:00:26.170
Me having a show.

00:00:26.170 --> 00:00:27.070
I was very shocked,

00:00:27.070 --> 00:00:29.180
but I'm still getting used
to being back in the studio.

00:00:29.180 --> 00:00:31.280
So is it true that you
guys, you've been at 30 Rock

00:00:31.280 --> 00:00:32.676
this whole time cause
you're the news, right?

00:00:32.676 --> 00:00:35.400
- What was weird I got to
tell you, it was super weird.

00:00:35.400 --> 00:00:39.260
I walked into 30 Rock the first
day and I almost like wept.

00:00:39.260 --> 00:00:40.710
You've been there a hundred times.

00:00:40.710 --> 00:00:43.090
Like the place's magic
comes from its density,

00:00:43.090 --> 00:00:45.760
from its people, from Rope, our cameraman,

00:00:45.760 --> 00:00:47.860
from Anthony, from our
floor director, Davey,

00:00:47.860 --> 00:00:51.060
like that's where you get the
juice and literally to hear

00:00:51.060 --> 00:00:53.810
your own footsteps and
to look at the desk,

00:00:53.810 --> 00:00:55.050
that's usually teeming with people

00:00:55.050 --> 00:00:57.090
and a place that's teeming with life.

00:00:57.090 --> 00:00:59.240
You know, usually we have
a million guests wandering

00:00:59.240 --> 00:01:02.000
around and you have celebs,
you got an orangutan

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:04.047
that's going to be on someone's
cooking something, you know,

00:01:04.047 --> 00:01:05.759
it's just all happening.

00:01:05.759 --> 00:01:08.879
And it was just so quiet
and it just, I think

00:01:08.879 --> 00:01:12.547
just the intensity of it just struck me.

00:01:12.547 --> 00:01:15.337
You sit, you mic up and
then you would just go

00:01:15.337 --> 00:01:18.350
and you feel like, and I know everyone

00:01:18.350 --> 00:01:20.700
at home felt the same way
who were reporting from home.

00:01:20.700 --> 00:01:23.280
You just feel like you're
all by yourself, weirdly.

00:01:23.280 --> 00:01:26.160
And the first words out of
your mouth happened to be to a,

00:01:26.160 --> 00:01:29.284
you know, a fellow anchor in Miami.

00:01:29.284 --> 00:01:34.070
And I think every day, Kel that
it got a little bit better.

00:01:34.070 --> 00:01:35.060
Like I remember I thought, well,

00:01:35.060 --> 00:01:37.120
I could take a nap on Broadway and no one,

00:01:37.120 --> 00:01:38.935
I could sleep there for
hours and no one would,

00:01:38.935 --> 00:01:40.676
would drive by.

00:01:40.676 --> 00:01:43.085
And I have to say fast
forward to now, man,

00:01:43.085 --> 00:01:44.810
I look out our window.

00:01:44.810 --> 00:01:47.540
Whenever we saw someone walk
by our window on the world,

00:01:47.540 --> 00:01:48.650
like, I didn't care who it was.

00:01:48.650 --> 00:01:51.920
I would, I would scream like,
wait, don't go, hold on.

00:01:51.920 --> 00:01:53.800
Cause we want to get a shot of somebody,

00:01:53.800 --> 00:01:55.769
a person walking by,

00:01:55.769 --> 00:01:57.230
a soul.

00:01:57.230 --> 00:01:59.430
And it was so empty and literally nurses

00:01:59.430 --> 00:02:00.400
would come by Kelly.

00:02:00.400 --> 00:02:02.990
They were on their way to their
shift and just stand there

00:02:02.990 --> 00:02:05.710
with signs that said that
they miss their kids.

00:02:05.710 --> 00:02:09.077
You know, it was, it was
moving, it was emotional.

00:02:09.077 --> 00:02:12.410
But I think it was like New
York and a lot of cities

00:02:12.410 --> 00:02:13.470
at their finest.

00:02:13.470 --> 00:02:14.303
- Yeah.

00:02:14.303 --> 00:02:16.420
You're right though, man, the
Today Show, it is always like,

00:02:16.420 --> 00:02:18.430
like beautiful chaos.

00:02:18.430 --> 00:02:20.350
Like there are so many things happening.

00:02:20.350 --> 00:02:23.450
So I can't imagine how that
would have maybe like affected

00:02:23.450 --> 00:02:24.900
you, like emotionally, just sitting there

00:02:24.900 --> 00:02:26.450
and mentally like your game,

00:02:26.450 --> 00:02:27.638
like and how you did your job.

00:02:27.638 --> 00:02:30.570
That's weird for it to be so, so bare.

